---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const lastUpdated = '2026-06-26';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Rackula"
  description="Rackula's privacy stance: self-hosted analytics, no third-party trackers, no accounts, your layouts stay in your browser."
>
  <article class="privacy">
    <div class="privacy__container">
      <h1 class="privacy__title">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="privacy__updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2 class="privacy__heading">The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Rackula doesn't track you across the web, doesn't sell anything, and
        doesn't want your data. The marketing site (here) uses self-hosted
        analytics that respect Do Not Track. The app (<a href="https://count.racku.la">count.racku.la</a>)
        keeps your rack layouts in your browser's localStorage — there are no
        accounts and no server-side storage of your plans.
      </p>

      <h2 class="privacy__heading">Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This site is measured with <a href="https://umami.is">Umami</a>, self-hosted
        on our own infrastructure. It collects aggregate, anonymised pageview
        counts — no cookies, no fingerprinting, no cross-site tracking. We honour
        your browser's Do Not Track setting.
      </p>

      <h2 class="privacy__heading">The app</h2>
      <p>
        Rackula the app runs client-side. Your rack layouts, device libraries,
        and history live in your browser's localStorage. Clearing your browser
        storage clears your data. Nothing about your rack is sent to any server.
      </p>

      <h2 class="privacy__heading">Self-hosting</h2>
      <p>
        Run it on your own hardware and none of the above even applies — your
        data stays entirely on your network. See the
        <a href="https://docs.racku.la/self-hosting">self-hosting guide</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="privacy__heading">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this? Open an issue on
        <a href="https://github.com/RackulaLives/Rackula">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy { padding: var(--space-16) var(--space-4); background-color: var(--colour-bg-primary); }
  .privacy__container { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .privacy__title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-4xl); color: var(--colour-text-primary); margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); }
  .privacy__updated { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--colour-text-secondary); margin: 0 0 var(--space-8); }
  .privacy__heading { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--text-xl); color: var(--colour-pink); margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-3); }
  .privacy p { color: var(--colour-text-primary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .privacy a { color: var(--colour-link); }
  .privacy a:hover { color: var(--colour-link-hover); }
</style>